WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:24.649
When I wrote about Jim Dooley
in Lisey’s Story, I was thinking

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:28.236
very much of the man
who shot John Lennon,

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:30.572
because this guy was a fan.

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:35.618
He was a huge fan of Lennon’s and
before shooting him to death,

00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:40.582
he got Lennon to sign an album
and I thought to myself,

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:42.500
yeah, I can see that happening.

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:48.757
Dooley really looks at Scott’s novels
as like scripture, you know,

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:50.675
he lives by them, he breathes them.

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:51.885
They’re everything to him.

00:00:55.972 --> 00:00:58.892
There was a lot of conversations
between Pablo and Stephen

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:03.104
and ultimately myself about
what to do with this character

00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:06.107
and adding scenes to
make him something

00:01:06.107 --> 00:01:08.610
more relatable and more real.

00:01:09.277 --> 00:01:14.449
Dane is a very gifted actor that
can make a very simple sort of

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:17.702
regular scene into something very

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:20.330
complicated, just by his presence. 

00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:26.753
It’s easy to play a strong rock
villain that is just a mean person.

00:01:28.546 --> 00:01:30.965
I think what Dane did so
beautifully is that he

00:01:30.965 --> 00:01:37.764
was also able to create a fragile
man in this context of the villain.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.600
And the fragility makes him vulnerable.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.270
And that vulnerability, it's
fascinating because it's hard.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.658
Prof.

00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:58.993
This is amazing and it’s
only the tip of the iceberg,

00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:00.995
there’s plenty more just waiting for us.

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:04.040
Look whatever it is I need you to stop.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.375
Listen, listen, listen,

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:07.710
there’s a story in here about
a father and his two sons.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.796
I’m pretty sure it’s the prequel
to The Coasters Daughter

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.381
he talked about it one time on NPR.

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:14.884
He’s fantastic. When
people read this they’re…

00:02:14.884 --> 00:02:16.052
Where did you get it?

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:20.140
She gave it to me. Easy as pie.

00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:23.476
Told you I was good
at persuading people.

